<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12387" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδάκνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bite off a piece of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristomen.
					14
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλα ἀποδεδηγμένα</span>”
				<i>with pieces bitten out,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tox.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			: also c. acc., <i>bite off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν αὑτῆς γλῶσσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polyaen.
					8.45
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>bite, gnaw,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδάξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					164
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				5.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Defix.Aud.</u>
				237.18
			</span></i> (Carthage, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>have one's tongue bitten,</i> as by a pungent
			substance, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				958b7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
